---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Playground from '../components/Playground.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Playground"
  active="play"
  description="Run the contract-ops CLIs in your browser — draft, compare, docx2pdf, and a template-vault explorer — on your own input, in a sandbox. No install, nothing stored."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Playground</p>
  <h1>Run the CLIs in your browser.</h1>

  <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100">
    Four of the suite's tools, running on <strong>your own input</strong> in a sandbox — no install,
    nothing stored. Switch tabs for <a href="/tools/draft-cli/">draft</a>,
    <a href="/tools/compare-cli/">compare</a>, <a href="/tools/docx2pdf-cli/">docx2pdf</a>, and the
    <a href="/tools/template-vault-cli/">template-vault</a> explorer.
  </p>

  <Callout label="How it works">
    Each run executes the real CLI server-side with strict limits — short timeout, rate-limited,
    a stripped environment, and ephemeral storage (your input is never kept). To see the tools
    chained end to end, take the <a href="/tour/">5-minute tour</a>.
  </Callout>

  <Playground height="660px" title="contract-ops playground" />

  <p>
    Two more tools have their own hosted demos: <a href="/tools/nda-review-cli/">nda-review-cli</a>
    (paste an NDA, get a structured review) and <a href="/tools/sign-cli/">sign-cli</a> (a read-only
    signing walkthrough).
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
